bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    seed_jit_f64_option_some_print_sink_reads_raw_payload_as_value_2026-11-27, 0, "Repro (aarch64 JIT, base e2479b4127a0a3a9 and the typed-reader fix): val c: f64? = Some(0.1); print c prints Option::Some(<denormal>) and print "interp {c}" prints Option::Some(<enum@0x...>); interpreter prints Option::Some(0.1) for both. The flat-optional print sink (rt_opt_value_to_string, lowering_expr_builtin.rs) formats the Option enum payload as a tagged RuntimeValue, but an explicit typed float Some holds the raw IEEE bits. rt_option_float_bits (value/objects.rs + runtime_native.c) already decodes all three float-optional forms exactly and could feed the sink."

